{"id": 6, "ts": 1779244578.4620395, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I am provisionally favoring **Candidate\u202fA** for the long\u2011distance pilot role.\n**Key evidence supporting A**\n- **Reliability & safety foresight:** \u201ccan anticipate dangerous situations\u201d and \u201cable to see complex connections,\u201d indicating strong situational awareness and proactive risk management.\n- **Technical competence:** \u201cexcellent spatial vision,\u201d essential for navigation and situational awareness on long routes.\n- **Teamwork & leadership:** \u201cvery good leadership qualities,\u201d suggesting ability to coordinate crew and make decisive calls.\n**Evidence that tempers A\u2019s profile**\n- **Potential crew\u2011relation issues:** regarded as a \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d and \u201cnot open to new ideas,\u201d which could affect morale and willingness to adopt new procedures.\n- **Missing explicit data:** no direct statements about calmness under pressure or decision\u2011making speed, both critical for long\u2011haul operations.\n**Major alternatives & trade\u2011offs**\n- **Candidate\u202fB** is highly conscientious, handles stress well, and excels in weather assessment, but his \u201cnasty remarks about colleagues\u201d and weak numeric memory raise serious teamwork and safety concerns.\n- **Candidate\u202fC** makes quick, correct decisions and stays calm in crises, yet his communication difficulties, egocentric attitude, and lack of willingness to continue education undermine crew cooperation and long\u2011term development.\n- **Candidate\u202fD** solves problems exceptionally and takes responsibility seriously, but his \u201chot temper,\u201d arrogance, and weak leadership suggest potential breakdowns in crew dynamics under pressure.\n**Remaining uncertainties**\n- How does Candidate\u202fA actually perform under high\u2011stress or unexpected events?\n- Does Candidate\u202fA possess the quick decision